WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:11.200
Before the dawn of creation, Sree Maha Vishu rested upon Ananta in eternal contemplation. Whenever dharma fades, Sree Maha Vishu descends.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:19.200
When furious waters dissolved the earth, Matsya the Divine Fish guided the sacred boat, preserving life and the eternal Vedas.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:28.500
As gods and demons churned the cosmic ocean, Kurma the Divine Tortoise bore Mount Mandara upon His back to steady creation.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:38.500
Plunging into the dark primal abyss, Varaha lifted Mother Earth upon His divine tusks, restoring Her to eternal light.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:48.500
Bursting forth from the shattered pillar, the fierce Man-Lion Narasimha destroyed arrogance and shielded unwavering devotion.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:58.500
Measuring the universe in three cosmic strides, the divine youth Vamana taught that true humility surpasses all earthly power.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:08.500
Wielding the sacred battle-axe of righteousness, Parashurama punished corrupt tyranny and decreed power must obey dharma.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:18.500
Mariyada Purushottama Sri Rama sacrificed all worldly comfort, demonstrating that dharma and truth must triumph at any cost.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:28.500
On the battlefield of Kurukshetra, Bhagavan Krishna unveiled the Bhagavad Gita, the immortal beacon of divine wisdom.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:38.500
Forsaking the illusions of power and war, Buddha illuminated the path of profound peace, boundless compassion, and truth.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:48.500
Riding the blazing white steed Devadatta, Kalki descends to conquer darkness and herald the golden dawn of renewal.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:00.500
Ten divine descents across the cosmic wheel of time. Sree Maha Vishu protects the universe. Dharma will rise again. Om Namo Narayanaya.

